>I have found a reference to a topic presented by A.H. Kadish at the
> 1968 DECUS Fall Symposium. Could someone please point me in the right
> direction of how I might go about finding a copy of the proceedings?
> Thanks~
>

You might try asking Encompass, the successor organization to DECUS 
(www.encompassus.org).  They "should" have archives.

Also, ask on the DECUServe system.  If you don't have an account, you can 
get one (free) by telnetting to eisner.decus.org, logging in as REGISTRATION 
(no password), and signing up for an instant account.  The system uses DEC 
Notes as a conferencing tool, and the "1st Aide" or "Shop_Talk" conferences 
would be appropriate places to ask - or just pick any conference in your 
notebook, for that matter.




